ut_transition.json","evidence_class":"semantic_validator","fresh_run_status":"not_run_by_index","historical_receipt_refs":["receipts/second_wave/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime/continuation_packet.json","receipts/second_wave/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime/heartbeat.json","receipts/second_wave/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime/resource_pressure.json","receipts/second_wave/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime/resume_receipt.json","receipts/second_wave/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime/closeout_transition.json"],"receipt_time_basis":"historical_saved_artifact"},"formal_subclaim_ids":[],"primary_guide_id":"paper_module.bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","primary_guide_ref":"paper_modules/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime.md","registered_runner_ref":"src/microcosm_core/organs/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime.py","replay_id":"replay::bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","requirements_review":{"status":"unrecorded"},"summary":"Checks synthetic continuation, heartbeat and resume records.","title":"Check a synthetic bridge continuation"},"claim_ceiling":"validates only declared public synthetic bridge-continuity fixtures over continuation packets, heartbeat boundaries, resource-pressure dispatch blocks, resume-once semantics, duplicate-resume rejection, worker-skip dedupe, closeout receipts, tracked receipt-write gates, negative cases, and private-state scan boundaries; does not run live bridge transport, call providers, read operator HUD/browser/phase-runtime/private-memory state, prove provider or UI uptime, land work, mutate source, authorize private-root equivalence, release, publication, or whole-system correctness","claim_ceiling_restated":"Checks a synthetic detached job, continuation packet, pressure record and heartbeats and writes five receipts, rejecting a duplicate resume and a heartbeat used as permission to resume.","claim_id":"claim::bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","evidence_class":"semantic_validator","evidence_strength_rank":5,"organ_id":"bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_import_validation","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.bridge_phase_continuity_runtime run --input fixtures/second_wave/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime/input --out receipts/second_wave/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"149cd222981083e068ab254c65322dedab34b6e5749d323c8720cd54406f4928","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"semantic_validator","family":"work_landing_and_continuity","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_import_validation"},"component_id":"bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","plain":"Resuming a paused job goes wrong if its resume note is missing or already used. This component reads made-up records of a paused job, its resume note, alive signals, computer-load decisions and skipped workers. It checks that the job paused with its place saved, its note is unused, and a recent alive signal matches the job's stage. It writes five saved records for testing handoff rules, and other cases catch a missing note, a second resume attempt and a stale alive signal that claims too much.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime.md","sha256":"0b020d4ff8ffe87fe86544a9be3cc92fda1453a0b4b5ea6cae5a1f1ce5fe3327","text":"# Check a synthetic bridge continuation\n\n> **In plain terms.** Resuming a paused job goes wrong if its resume note is missing or already used. This component reads made-up records of a paused job, its resume note, alive signals, computer-load decisions and skipped workers. It checks that the job paused with its place saved, its note is unused, and a recent alive signal matches the job's stage. It writes five saved records for testing handoff rules, and other cases catch a missing note, a second resume attempt and a stale alive signal that claims too much.\n\n`bridge_phase_continuity_runtime` reads a synthetic detached job, continuation packet, heartbeat rows, resource-pressure decisions and worker-skip records. The continuation packet identifies the job to resume and records whether the packet has already been consumed. The validator checks whether the supplied records describe a coherent continuation and writes five JSON receipts. This is useful for testing handoff rules without running a bridge.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root, with Python 3.11 or later:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.bridge_phase_continuity_runtime run \\\n  --input fixtures/second_wave/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime/input \\\n  --out .microcosm/component-guides/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime\n```\n\nInspect `closeout_transition.json` for findings and the other four files for continuation, heartbeat, pressure and resume details. The input also references a source manifest; the validator checks the listed copied modules against their digests.\n\n## What this checks\n\nThe positive job must have yielded to disk, reference an unconsumed packet, and have a fresh heartbeat with compatible phase and continuity identifiers. Other fixture cases exercise missing packets, duplicate resume attempts and stale heartbeat overclaims. Tests change the supplied records to show the findings follow their contents. A heartbeat is evidence of a recorded liveness signal, not evidence that work landed.\n\n## Limits\n\nThe fixture is synthetic. It does not connect to a live bridge, dispatch a provider or establish that a real handoff succeeded. Matching source hashes shows that copies match their manifest, not that their algorithms are correct.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe direct example does not invoke the shared gate. In `make component-replays`, this component’s registered route passes through the [Dafny replay admission check](../formal/replay/README.md), which checks source, input, claim-policy and receipt agreement over host-supplied observations. It does not prove this component’s algorithm.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime.py), [input files](../fixtures/second_wave/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime/input) and [tests](../tests/test_bridge_phase_continuity_runtime.py).\n- [Historical closeout result](../receipts/second_wave/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime/closeout_transition.json) and [component record](../core/paper_module_capsules.json).\n- [Temporal durable execution](https://docs.temporal.io/) and [W3C PROV](https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-overview/) provide wider workflow and provenance context.\n"},"proofs":[],"replay":{"command":"make component-replays","command_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_replays.py","command_scope":"all registered components","configuration_refs":["src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#RUNTIME_STEPS","src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#_accepted_organ_runner_module_refs"],"declared_prerequisites":{"availability_status":"not_assessed_by_index","description":"Lean, Swift and test extras required","source_ref":"Makefile"},"execution_status":"not_run_by_index","fresh_receipt_template":".microcosm/component-replays/<run>/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime/closeout_transition.json","guide_example":{"command":"microcosm bridge-phase-continuity-runtime run --input fixtures/second_wave/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime/input --out /tmp/microcosm-bridge-continuity","expected_result_description":{"status":"unrecorded"},"prerequisites_description":{"see":"paper_modules/bridge_phase_continuity_runtime.md","status":"unrecorded"},"scope":"verbatim historical Atlas example; not an execution request and may target retained receipt paths","sour